From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: stand-ins for icon glyphs Windows Terminal uses

Windows Terminal draws eight more Segoe MDL2 Assets / Segoe Fluent Icons glyphs that had no standard character to stand in for them when the icon font is missing (since 6226 they were left out): RevToggleKey, ZoomIn, ChevronRightMed, ErrorBadge and the four CaretSolid8 arrows (names from the public Segoe MDL2 Assets icon list). They now draw as standard characters the stand-in font has. Lock, Shield, Ringer and NetworkTower still have none (no fitting character in DejaVu Sans). +xamltree also shows each element's BorderBrush.
---
diff --git a/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/glyphs.txt b/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/glyphs.txt
index 46de9a2..583508c 100644
--- a/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/glyphs.txt
+++ b/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/glyphs.txt
@@ -25,24 +25,32 @@ Up E74A 2191
 Down E74B 2193
 Delete E74D 232B
 Save E74E 21E9
-ChevronLeft E76B 2039
-ChevronRight E76C 203A
 Play E768 25B6
 Pause E769 2016
-Warning E7BA 26A0
+ChevronLeft E76B 2039
+ChevronRight E76C 203A
 Error E783 2297
+Warning E7BA 26A0
 Home E80F 2302
-Help E897 003F
+RevToggleKey E845 21C4
